    "result_text": "Done. The build is green.\n\nI implemented the audit requirement in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`. On a successful create \u2014 after `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2014 the controller now emits one line via a dedicated SLF4J logger named `AUDIT` carrying the owner id, the `customerCode`, and the `registrationDate`:\n\n```\nINFO  AUDIT - Owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-07\n```\n\nChanges to `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n- Added `org.slf4j.Logger`/`LoggerFactory` imports and a `private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`.\n- Logged the audit line only after the save succeeds (so rejected requests \u2014 validation, quota, conflict \u2014 produce no audit entry), and after `customerCode`/`registrationDate` are set on the owner.\n\nThe acceptance test `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` passes and the full suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
